What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.13?
This release is API and ABI compatible with 0.31.12 (libautotrace.so.3).

Security:
- a fatal error while curves were fitted freed the background colour
  twice (GHSA-7qjh-rrv3-frfw).  Only library clients whose message
  handler returns after a fatal error could get there; the autotrace
  program exits first.

Tracing:
- a border shared by two colour regions is fitted once and used by
  both, so no seams or white cracks show along it (#338).
- much faster: messages for -log debug are no longer formatted when
  they won't be shown (#370), and the autotrace program finds corners
  and fits curves on several threads, one per processor or as many as
  AUTOTRACE_THREADS says (#155).  The output doesn't depend on the number
  of threads.  Library clients still get one thread.
- with -background-color, the holes of anti-aliased shapes are kept, so
  an anti-aliased ring no longer comes out as a disc (#379).  The FIG
  writer fills holes with the background colour instead of white
  (#383), and the Sketch writer cuts them out (#381).

Centerline tracing:
- right-angle corners are kept, so a square traces as four straight
  sides (#50).
- the points lie on the pixel centres; they were half a pixel off, in
  opposite directions on x and y (#366).
- in colour images, strokes along the image border are traced as in
  grey ones; they were lost or pulled onto the border (#390).

Library:
- at_splines_new_full() returns NULL, as documented, when it is
  cancelled or fails before fitting, instead of an uninitialised
  result (#372).

Other changes:
- the manual page and -help say what the despeckling options actually
  do (#376).
- tests/corpus/ compares the traces of two builds, for pull requests
  that change traced output.  It measures them against the source image
  and, for the synthetic images, against the shapes drawn (#341, #387).

What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.12?
This release is API and ABI compatible with 0.31.11 (libautotrace.so.3).

Security:
- images wider or taller than 65535 pixels overflowed a heap buffer in
  the ImageMagick/GraphicsMagick and PNM readers, and in the PNG reader
  of 0.31.11; they are now rejected (GHSA-f57q-wgfx-9vp3).  So are such
  BMP images, which were cropped.
- GF fonts whose characters paint or move outside their bounding box
  wrote past a heap buffer; they are now rejected (GHSA-4cx5-xpv3-hqq5).

Reading images:
- ImageMagick 6 and GraphicsMagick: 16-bit images lost the high byte of
  every sample and got wrong colours (#359).
- the ImageMagick/GraphicsMagick reader reads whole rows, reports a
  failed pixel read instead of tracing whatever the buffer held, and is
  faster (#340).
- files ending in .tif, or in any other suffix ImageMagick or
  GraphicsMagick doesn't register, or with no suffix, are read by the
  *Magick reader, which detects the format from the content (#360).

Other changes:
- -list-input-formats and -list-output-formats line up the descriptions
  when a suffix is longer than five characters (#339).
- the test suite passes with ImageMagick builds whose policy.xml limits
  the image size, as on Ubuntu 22.04 (#362).

What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.11?
This release is API and ABI compatible with 0.31.10 (libautotrace.so.3).

Packaging and platforms:
- the Windows installers (win32 and win64) contain the real autotrace.exe
  again; those of 0.31.10 shipped libtool's wrapper script, which exited
  with status 127 and printed nothing (#223).  They are now built by CI
  for every tag.
- works with pstoedit 4.x; 0.31.10 printed "wrong version of pstoedit"
  and disabled the pstoedit formats (#159, #213).
- libautotrace.so is linked against the libraries it uses, so programs
  can link with just `pkg-config --libs autotrace` or load it with
  dlopen() (#124, #324).
- autotrace.pc: the Magick libraries are substituted for static linking,
  and GLib 2.58 is required, as by configure (#160, #325).
- requires GLib >= 2.58 and a C17 compiler.  Translations moved from
  intltool to plain GNU gettext and to Weblate; new: Brazilian
  Portuguese, Italian, Spanish, Simplified Chinese, Tamil, Georgian.
- removed: SWF output (libming, #137) and the native macOS installer;
  install from Homebrew or MacPorts instead.

Reading images:
- native BMP reader: RLE4/RLE8, 2 bpp, 32 bpp with an alpha mask and
  grey-palette images were traced as garbage (#319, #320, #321); pixels
  with an index beyond the palette, and grey palettes, read uninitialised
  memory, which could reach the output (GHSA-75xg-mchm-ch42).  Top-down
  BMPs are read.
- the BMP and TGA readers crashed library callers whose message handler
  returns when the input file could not be opened (#322).
- PNG: transparent pixels are composited against the background (#97).
- GraphicsMagick: an uninitialised exception structure was passed to
  AcquireOnePixel() (#323).
- malformed GF fonts are reported instead of terminating the program.

Tracing and output:
- -despeckle no longer overflows the stack on large regions (#154), and
  -error-threshold 0 no longer recurses without bound (#247).
- the library no longer calls exit() or changes the host program's
  locale; real-valued options are parsed in the C locale.
- "-" writes to standard output, and binary formats written to standard
  output are no longer corrupted on Windows.
- SVG honours -preserve-width; DXF puts each shape on the layer of its
  colour; MIF colours each object with its own colour; DR2D stores the
  line thickness.
- invalid -background-color values are rejected; output files are created
  with mode 0644.

What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.2?
- improved spec file(Dag Wieers).
- gettextized (Masatake(ja), Martin(de)).
- povray output support(Martin).

What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.1?
- fixed compile time error appeared when an user 
  specifies --without-pstoedit option(Ralf Stubner).
- fixed a bug related to centerline tracing(Martin).
- fixed bugs in dr2d output and dxf output(Martin).
- changed the name of tracing option structure
  field(width_weight_factor)(Masatake). This means 
  source compatibility is broken.

What's new in AutoTrace 0.31.0?
(This NEWS items are the summary of changed from 0.30.1 to 0.30.8)
- improved interface between pstoedit and autotrace
- added library level pstoedit support
- built autotrace library as a shared library
- corrected output when background-color is used
- changing the license of sources files input and output 
  to GNU Lesser Public License(LGPL)
- checking libautotrace version number in autotrace.m4
- output in dr2d format(Andrew Elia)
- introduced config.h
- corrected thin-image
- made more portable
- corrected a bug in fitting
- now recognizes line width

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.8?
- added variable line width in centerline tracing(--width-factor, --preserve-width)
  autotrace library API is changed.
- fixed memory leaks
- many bugs fixes

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.6?
- added workaround for a compile time error that appears when 
  autotrace is linked to pstoedit-3.32.0.
- made code that creates temporary file more portable.

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.5?
- fixed a compile time error that appears when autotrace 
  is not linked to pstoedit.

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.4?
- fixed a bug reported by Gerhard Gaussling <ggrubbish@web.de>
- improved the interface between pstoedit and autotrace

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.2?
- added library level pstoedit support
- built autotrace library as a shared library

What's new in AutoTrace 0.30.1?
